{
 "screen": "store",
 "source": "store.png + store_2.png",
 "canvas": [
  941,
  1672
 ],
 "ground": "#09151E",
 "notes": [
  "The Royal Store as a Court view (client/scenes/court/store_view.gd), cut from art/reference/store.png and store_2.png (art/slices/store.json, store_2.json). The two paintings are one page: the header stays, and every section under it scrolls, stacked in the paintings' order 10 units apart (both paintings space their panels so). A section with nothing to show -- no live offer, Herald's Tidings while this server has no adverts -- is left out and the rest close up.",
  "Section templates: rect x is from the scroll's left edge (x 155), y is 0 (the view stacks them); every part is relative to its section's own crop. Section crops are cut tight to their panels, so the panels sit on the view's ground as they sit on the paintings'.",
  "Prices are the App Store's own (Billing.price), set on the painted green buttons in the Shop's price type (body 700). A button whose price is not known yet, or on a phone without StoreKit, is dimmed; the note line under the header then says Billing.NOT_HERE.",
  "Diamond packs: the six arts are drawn in the catalogue's order, the ribboned ones (MOST POPULAR, BEST VALUE) for the products whose badge says so, so a ribbon always names the pack it is on. pack_art_rows says which of the painting's two rows an art was cut from: row b's plate and button sit 6 and 7 units lower, and the third column's 2 units right (dx). The x2 FIRST PURCHASE seal (store/seal) is drawn on every pack whose first purchase still pays double.",
  "Daily deals keep the painting's four pictures; the fourth slot shows the Splendour cosmetic it sells in cosmetic_box (a crest, a colour chip, or the painted frame for a frame this build has no picture of)."
 ],
